%N A034021 Numbers that are primitively but not imprimitively represented by x^2+xy+y^2.
%C A034021 Also numbers that are squarefree and primitively represented by x^2+x*y+y^2. - _Frank M Jackson_, Nov 08 2013
%C A034021 For n > 1, all a(n) are the squarefree integers whose prime factorization contains only primes of the form 3 Union {p |p is prime and p is congruent to 1 (mod 6)}. - _Frank M Jackson_, Jun 29 2026
%C A034021 Union of {0} and the squarefree Loesch numbers. - _Hugo Pfoertner_, Sep 16 2026
%H A034021 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A034021/b034021.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A034021 lst = {}; Do[k=x^2+x*y+y^2; If[(SquareFreeQ[k] && GCD[x, y]==1) || k==0, AppendTo[lst, k]], {x, 0, 100}, {y, 0, x}]; Union@lst (* _Frank M Jackson_, Nov 08 2013 *)
%o A034021 (PARI) \\ Uses any of the functions given in A003136
%o A034021 is_a034021(n) = !n || (issquarefree(n) && is_a003136(n)) \\ _Hugo Pfoertner_, Sep 16 2026
%Y A034021 Cf. A034017, A003136, A045897.
